\tag{fdip}
\title{Clustering from a finite-volume comparison}
\date{2026-11-09}

\p{The invariant state of \ref{fdip-00I6} has the regularity and
positive reflected form needed for reconstruction. Uniqueness of the
vacuum requires information about widely separated observables.
Can a bound proved for a periodic comparison law control those
correlations in this particular half-Dirichlet limit?}

